<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">10 February in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 10 February, from 1258 to 1989.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/baghdad.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1258">1258 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">768 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Baghdad surrenders to the Mongols</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After a short siege, the Abbasid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">Caliph</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-mustasim">al-Musta'sim</a> surrendered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hulagu-khan">Hulagu Khan</a>. The city was sacked and the Caliph executed days later, ending five centuries of Abbasid rule from Baghdad.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasid Caliphate</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hulagu-khan">Hulagu Khan</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1306">1306 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">720 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Robert the Bruce kills John Comyn at Dumfries</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Bruce stabbed his rival for the Scottish crown before the altar of Greyfriars church. Committed to rebellion, he was crowned King of Scots weeks later and defeated the English at Bannockburn in 1314.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1763">1763 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">263 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Treaty of Paris ends the Seven Years' War</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> ceded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a> and lands east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> gave up <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a>. Britain emerged as the leading colonial power, though France kept its trading posts in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/british-empire">British Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seven-years-war">Seven Years' War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1840">1840 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">186 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Queen Victoria marries Prince Albert</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Victoria married her cousin Albert of Saxe-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coburg">Coburg</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gotha">Gotha</a> at the Chapel Royal, St James's Palace. Her white wedding dress set a lasting fashion; Albert became her closest adviser.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1906">1906 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">120 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">HMS Dreadnought is launched</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">King Edward VII launched the battleship at Portsmouth. With ten 12-inch guns and steam turbines, she made existing battleships obsolete and intensified the naval race with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1940">1940 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">86 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Soviet Union begins mass deportations from eastern Poland</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nkvd">NKVD</a> deported some 140,000 Polish citizens, many of them families of settlers and foresters, to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siberia">Siberia</a> and Kazakhstan. It was the first of four <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deportation">mass deportations</a> in 1940-41.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siberia">Siberia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1962">1962 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">64 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">U-2 pilot Gary Powers exchanged for Soviet spy Rudolf Abel</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">On the Glienicke Bridge between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-berlin">West Berlin</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/potsdam">Potsdam</a>, the US pilot shot down in 1960 was swapped for the KGB colonel Rudolf Abel. The bridge became known for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cold-war">Cold War</a> exchanges.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1989">1989 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">37 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Ron Brown becomes the first Black chairman of a major US party</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Ron Brown was elected chairman of the Democratic National Committee. He helped Bill Clinton win in 1992 and became Secretary of Commerce before dying in a plane crash in 1996.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 10 February <span class="n">5</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/christine-of-france"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/christine-of-france.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Christine of France</span><span class="tp">1606–1663</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/boris-pasternak"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/boris-pasternak.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Boris Pasternak</span><span class="tp">1890–1960</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/arpad-goncz"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/arpad-goncz.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Árpád Göncz</span><span class="tp">1922–2015</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/luis-donaldo-colosio"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Luis Donaldo Colosio</span><span class="tp">1950–1994</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/lee-hsien-loong"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/lee-hsien-loong.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Lee Hsien Loong</span><span class="tp">b. 1952</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 10 February <span class="n">3</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/baldwin-iii-of-jerusalem"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/baldwin-iii-of-jerusalem.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Baldwin III of Jerusalem</span><span class="tp">1130–1163</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/frederick-ii-elector-of-brandenburg"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/frederick-ii-elector-of-brandenburg.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Frederick II, Elector of Brandenburg</span><span class="tp">1413–1471</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/pope-pius-xi"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pope-pius-xi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Pope Pius XI</span><span class="tp">1857–1939</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
